A||||4||MooCow||Need a lot of Opinions Fast!||||1||
Z||000000||MooCow||10-15-2000||07:50 PM||||Okay as some of you may know I am possibly either going to Ed Parks or to Twin Lake Fiero's to trade my 4-speed stick to an auto Fiero because I hate sticks.  Now my problem is, should I switch Fieros and then next year when I actaully take it out to drive make it into a GT?  Or should I just sell my Fiero now and then next year just buy a GT?  I kinda sorta want a GT but then at times I don't.  I know I want an Auto.  Someone please help this 18 year old out before I rip my hair out.<P>                           Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||10-15-2000||08:11 PM||||Depends. I think if you really are sure you want a GT. I would buy a GT. You could always buy a non-running GT and use it to convert your car to GT. I am going to rebuild my GT in Jan and remove the rust. I am giving myself 3 months to do it, and it might take longer. If you are up for it, try and convert it, but if your not ready or willing for that much work, buy a GT.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||10-15-2000||08:18 PM||||Before I really got into Fieros, I kind of favored the fastback look, because they look so good in pictures. But after seeing the fastbacks up close and in real life, I don't really like them. Plus, it seems like everyone and their brother is after a fastback. I have always been one who doesn't like to "follow the crowd", so the more people search for a fastback, the more I search for a notchback. Plus, the notchback is one sweet looking machine.<P>I don't know what Bob quoted you, but when I was getting pricing for my poly bushing installation, I remember Bob pricing more than 3 times what Ed Parks wanted, for the exact same work, plus I trust Ed more than any other Fiero guy in the world.<P>I say go with the Fiero you want. You really don't want a stick, huh? Well, what are your plans for that Muncie you plan to have removed? I might want it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||10-15-2000||08:37 PM||||In 1987 when I got my GT it had to be the 5 speed.  I mean if you're going to have a "sports car" why get an automatic.  But if you do any stop and go driving, an automatic is great.<P>Twin Lakes put in a heavy duty clutch in my 87 last winter and it drives great, until I got stuck in some Chicago stop and go traffic. Clutch, shift, clutch, shift for what seems like hours.  Don't get me wrong the transmission and clutch work flawlessly, but what a pain in stop and go traffic.  Also if you want to do street drags, you have to know how to shift quickly.<P>Benefits I get fantastic gas milage 30+ mpg on the highway and nothing sounds better than the Fiero rumble, when slowing down in 3rd gear.<P>I also have (had) a GT with with the T125 automatic transmission.  A real quick car that gets away from me.  Down side lousy gas milage over the road maybe 25 mpg. No nice rumble when slowing down. Twin Lakes is currently swaping a 3.4 and a T440 (four speed automatic) into that one.  I'll have to see how this turns out.<P>Personally, if you have the funds for an auto GT go for it. Ed Parks or Bob Steiger and there are other reliable Fiero dealers out there have auto GT's sitting on their lots. Bob or Ed would insure that the car would be in working condition. (As opposed to purchasing a car from a previous owner). As for modifying a coupe to a GT, it would be a learing experience and at 18 you have a lot to learn like college, and time will be at a minimum.  <BR>Keep in mind that any GT you buy is 12-15 years old and may be in need of some serious mechanical repair. Bob, Ed and some other know how to fix them, and have done several basket cases to get the cars back to shape.||||reg||3
Z||000004||2xsess||10-15-2000||09:09 PM||||Well, I've had both, sticks and autos. I like the stick better because of the feeling of control. The 2nd week I had my first suto GT I spun out on a turn and ended up on top of a rock wall.<BR>My opinion is if you have to wait to get what you really want then it's worth the wait.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
